 & ≡8\\cdot 0+1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we decompose ${29}^{13}$ into a product of smaller exponents. \n\n$$\n{29}^{13}={({29}^{2})}^{6}\\cdot 29\n$$\n\nBy applying the multiplicative and exponentiation properties, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{29}^{13} & ≡{({29}^{2})}^{6}\\cdot 29\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡(1)^{6}\\cdot 9\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡1\\cdot 9\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡9\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{29}^{13}\\text{ mod }10=9\n$$\n\nwhich means that the last digit of ${29}^{13}$ is $9.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d74f7ec1-3d25-58dd-8633-311ea5f4ae4f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d74f7ec1-3d25-58dd-8633-311ea5f4ae4f" :answer-field/id #uuid "d74f7ec1-3d25-58dd-8633-311ea5f4ae4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8e99904f-599e-570f-9b78-5cc24914671a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f7facb81-4920-5297-86bc-cd1ce30a844e" "answer-c358ed21-b0f9-58ea-96b0-9537635fff34" "answer-3114b013-db2a-5732-82d6-7346aac261fd" "answer-1354f5fe-aec3-598e-a11c-ecb2baf266d2" "answer-8e99904f-599e-570f-9b78-5cc24914671a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7facb81-4920-5297-86bc-cd1ce30a844e" :answer/id #uuid "f7facb81-4920-5297-86bc-cd1ce30a844e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c358ed21-b0f9-58ea-96b0-9537635fff34" :answer/id #uuid "c358ed21-b0f9-58ea-96b0-9537635fff34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3114b013-db2a-5732-82d6-7346aac261fd" :answer/id #uuid "3114b013-db2a-5732-82d6-7346aac261fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1354f5fe-aec3-598e-a11c-ecb2baf266d2" 